{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfkxihG23KhhaqDEmJnPZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017qqFRzZyutvxMR5jtUpkfE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_2\ncat > $D/hypothesis.md << 'EOF'\nThe choice is made by a Thurstonian comparison: each sequence's felt randomness is read with Gaussian internal noise, and the person picks whichever noisy impression is larger. Choice probability therefore follows a normal (probit) curve of the evidence difference instead of a logistic one, so its tails are thinner: on clear-cut pairs, such as a long pure streak against a sequence with one or two breaks, choices become close to deterministic, while near-ties stay graded. The evidence itself is unchanged from the current best account (the person's own second-order picture of a fair coin weighed against a switch-biased coin, a heads-favoured trick coin and a repeating motif with slips, per flip with pseudo-flip dilution, with heavy-tailed signed person sensitivity and a side habit). This addresses the FDR-surviving critique that people pick the more-switching sequence in long low-switch pairs more decisively than the logistic model predicts.\nEOF\necho thurstonian_probit_decision > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'EOF'\nD=\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_2\"\nsrc=open(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/models/short_sequence_pseudoflip_dilution.py\").read()\ndoc_new='''\"\"\"Thurstonian (Gaussian-noise, probit) decision rule on the incumbent's evidence.\n\nHypothesis: each sequence's felt randomness is read with Gaussian internal\nnoise and the larger noisy impression is chosen, so the choice probability is a\nnormal CDF of the evidence difference rather than a logistic. The probit's thin\ntails make clear-cut pairs (a long streak versus one with one or two breaks)\nnear-deterministic while near-ties stay graded. The evidence is exactly that of\n`short_sequence_pseudoflip_dilution` (described below); only the link changes:\np_left = Phi(0.588 * (eta + side)), the 0.588 factor matching the logistic's\nslope at zero so the priors keep their meaning. Addresses the FDR-surviving\ncritique that people choose the more-switching sequence in long low-switch\npairs more often than the logistic model predicts.\n\nDescription of the evidence model follows.\n\n'''\nsrc = src.replace('\"\"\"', doc_new, 1)\nold='    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\"p_left\", pm.math.sigmoid(eta + side[pid]))'\nnew='''    # Thurstonian decision rule: Gaussian noise on the impression difference.\n    dv = 0.588 * (eta + side[pid])\n    p_probit = 0.5 * pt.erfc(-dv / math.sqrt(2.0))\n    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\"p_left\", pt.clip(p_probit, 1e-6, 1.0 - 1e-6))'''\nassert old in src\nsrc=src.replace(old,new)\nopen(D+\"/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(src)\nEOF\nhead -20 $D/candidate.py\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8068,"cache_read_input_tokens":78902,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8068,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6396df9f-46a6-477c-b503-f92c7fc3cc60","uuid":"