{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FbjqSz2kJ3hUu9W7adpoBx","type":"tool_result","content":"   117       20:46  0.0 /bin/bash -c source /home/users/kushinm/.claude/shell-snapshots/snapshot-bash-1791288698300-gt3n2e.sh 2>/dev/null || true && shopt -u extglob 2>/dev/null || true && { \\builtin unalias -- 'unsetenv'; \\builtin unset -f -- 'unsetenv'; } >/dev/null 2>&1 || true && eval 'D=/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_2 cat > $D/hypothesis.md << '\"'\"'EOF'\"'\"' The choice is made by a Thurstonian comparison: each sequence'\"'\"'s felt randomness is read with Gaussian internal noise, and the person picks whichever noisy impression is larger. Choice probability therefore follows a normal (probit) curve of the evidence difference instead of a logistic one, so its tails are thinner: on clear-cut pairs, such as a long pure streak against a sequence with one or two breaks, choices become close to deterministic, while near-ties stay graded. The evidence itself is unchanged from the current best account (the person'\"'\"'s own second-order picture of a fair coin weighed against a switch-biased coin, a heads-favoured trick coin and a repeating motif with slips, per flip with pseudo-flip dilution, with heavy-tailed signed person sensitivity and a side habit). This addresses the FDR-surviving critique that people pick the more-switching sequence in long low-switch pairs more decisively than the logistic model predicts. EOF echo thurstonian_probit_decision > $D/model_name.txt python3 - << '\"'\"'EOF'\"'\"' D=\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_3/candidate_2\" src=open(\"/scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/models/short_sequence_pseudoflip_dilution.py\").read() doc_new='\"'\"''\"'\"''\"'\"'\"\"\"Thurstonian (Gaussian-noise, probit) decision rule on the incumbent'\"'\"'s evidence.  Hypothesis: each sequence'\"'\"'s felt randomness is read with Gaussian internal noise and the larger noisy impression is chosen, so the choice probability is a normal CDF of the evidence difference rather than a logistic. The probit'\"'\"'s thin tails make clear-cut pairs (a long streak versus one with one or two breaks) near-deterministic while near-ties stay graded. The evidence is exactly that of `short_sequence_pseudoflip_dilution` (described below); only the link changes: p_left = Phi(0.588 * (eta + side)), the 0.588 factor matching the logistic'\"'\"'s slope at zero so the priors keep their meaning. Addresses the FDR-surviving critique that people choose the more-switching sequence in long low-switch pairs more often than the logistic model predicts.  Description of the evidence model follows.  '\"'\"''\"'\"''\"'\"' src = src.replace('\"'\"'\"\"\"'\"'\"', doc_new, 1) old='\"'\"'    p_left = pm.Deterministic(\"p_left\", pm.math.sigmoid(eta + side[pid]))'\"'\"' new='\"'\"''\"'\"''\"'\"'    # Thurstonian decision rule: Gaussian noise on the impression difference.     dv = 0.588 * (eta + side[pid])     p_probit = 0.5 * pt.erfc(-dv / math.sqrt(2.0))     p_left = pm.Deterministic(\"p_left\", pt.clip(p_probit, 1e-6, 1.0 - 1e-6))'\"'\"''\"'\"''\"'\"' assert old in src src=src.replace(old,new) open(D+\"/candidate.py\",\"w\").write(src) EOF head -20 $D/candidate.py cd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir $D --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5' && pwd -P >| /tmp/claude-7581-cwd\n   122       20:46 87.5 /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir /scratch/use